From 286ae86efe7c9d58b99baeb83255b2b03ce4bb12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 02:25:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] soc: apple: add zero-traffic inherited A9 AOP ring reader

Discover exact v7 ring signatures in valid linear-mapped System RAM
with a root-only one-shot debugfs scan. Bound bytes, time, hit count
and read rate; abort on a synchronous copy fault. Exclude scanner
copies and the reading task's stack, distinguish discovery from the
two-second watch baseline, and report current page state without
claiming historical ownership. Warn loudly on candidates and advancing
rings in Linux allocator RAM.

Behind a separate immutable opt-in, accept only an early plain no-map
DT RAM reservation and map it normal WB read-only. Require a fresh
publication and bounded motion report before registering a minimal
direct-read IIO accelerometer. Use AOP signed 16.16 g report units,
retain firmware ARot, and return ENODATA when data stops. Never
acknowledge rptr; a producer that requires space reclamation may fill
the ring and stop.

Both ring opt-ins exclude active-driver probe and bypass all observer
wrapper/power access. Add no mailbox, FIFO, IRQ, reset, sensor, power,
cache-maintenance, shared-memory write or late reservation path.

Validate the const parser with host ASan/UBSan tests, wrap/publication
and malformed packet cases, and input immutability. Build arm64 with
LLVM=1 and W=1. Device streaming, coherency, physical scale and mount
orientation remain orchestrator tests; no device access was performed.

Signed-off-by: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
